{
  "id": "book-22",
  "checkpoint": 6,
  "title": "Crossing the Bridge",
  "summary": "Paul segue pela avenida principal em direção ao norte, atravessa a grande ponte sobre o rio e observa a movimentação da cidade.",
  "audio_url": "/audios/book-22.mp3",
  "word_count_target": 140,
  "story_en": "Paul follows the wide avenue toward the north. Many people walk along the sidewalks, and cars drive past in a steady rhythm. The morning air feels cool against his skin.\n\nSoon, he arrives at the stone bridge. Below, the clear water of the river flows smoothly toward the valley. Several boats rest near the riverbank.\n\nPaul stops in the middle of the bridge and leans on the iron rail. An older cyclist slows down beside him. “Nice view of the water, isn’t it?” the cyclist remarks with a warm grin.\n\n“It really is,” Paul agrees. “Is the train station straight ahead?”\n\n“Yes, keep going forward for two more blocks,” the cyclist explains. “You cannot miss the big clock tower.”\n\nPaul thanks the rider and continues his journey across the bridge.",
